{id:"treehouse-hideaway",name:"Grand Canopy Treehouse",emoji:"🌳",tags:["Nature","Fantasy","Showpiece"],diff:"Expert",time:"4 hr",size:"24×13",photos:[P6],pr:[1.299],photoCredit:"",desc:"A towering dark oak treehouse with a spiral staircase, an eight-sided cabin, a glowing leaf canopy, a copper-roofed crow’s nest and a bridge to a satellite pavilion.",steps:[
["Raise the great trunk","Stack a 3×3 column of dark oak logs 17 blocks tall. This is the spine of the whole build, so set it out first and mark the centre block.",[]],
["Wind the spiral stairs","Circle the trunk with a 5×5 ring of spruce stairs, climbing one block for every block you go around: 15 steps in all. Point each stair’s high side toward the next one. Prop the three corner steps on spruce fence posts so they don’t hang in mid-air.",[]],
["Lay the grand deck","At the top of the stairs, lay an eight-sided deck 13 blocks across: dark oak planks on the rim, spruce planks inside. Leave two holes above the last two steps for headroom and finish the landing with one spruce slab. Hold the deck up on four dark oak stilts, then add a spruce fence railing, leaving a 5-block gap on the east side for the bridge.",[]],
["Frame the cabin","Run the trunk up another 11 blocks through the middle. Around it, build an eight-sided cabin, 9 across and 4 tall: dark oak log posts, mossy stone bricks along the base, birch planks for the walls, glass panes for the windows and a dark oak plank beam on top. Leave a 1×2 doorway in the middle of the east wall.",[]],
["Stack the roof","Cap the cabin with a stepped roof that overhangs the walls by one block. Ring each layer with spruce stairs facing inward, fill the middle with dark oak planks and finish with a patch of moss block. Plant four flowering azalea leaves on top of the moss.",[]],
["Grow the canopy","Spread dark oak wood branches (the bark-on-every-side block) out from the trunk in four directions at the height of the roof peak, then add a side rail to each branch tip. Pack a cloud of leaves onto each of the eight points, mixing in flowering azalea, and tuck shroomlight underneath so the canopy glows from below.",[]],
["Top it with a crow’s nest","On top of the trunk, build a small eight-sided lookout, 7 across, with a spruce fence railing and four dark oak posts. Roof it in copper: weathered copper first, then oxidized copper stepping in to a peak, and finish with a lightning rod. A ladder up the side of the trunk gets you there; it isn’t shown in the 3D view.",[]],
["Span the bridge","Run a 6-block spruce bridge east from the gap in the railing, with fence rails on both sides, to a 5×5 satellite pavilion. Hold the pavilion up on a single dark oak wood trunk, then give it corner posts, railings and its own small stepped roof topped with moss and an azalea.",[]],
["Light and furnish","Hang eight lanterns from chains under the edge of the main roof, one more under the pavilion roof, and one inside the crow’s nest. Stand six lanterns on the railing along the deck and bridge. Inside the cabin, set bookshelves against the west wall and barrels beside the door. Finally, spread moss block around both trunks and scatter mossy cobblestone boulders and azalea bushes.",[]]]},
